invariant: INV-74
file: src/tcp_seal.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: ch_close_out seals close_notify at level 2, fatal, so the peer
  reads a fatal alert and fails its session, where RFC 9846 §6.1 makes
  close_notify a closure alert that leaves the peer's direction open.

--- old
    int rc = tlsi_seal_alert(t, 1, ALERT_CLOSE_NOTIFY, out, out_len);
--- new
    int rc = tlsi_seal_alert(t, 2, ALERT_CLOSE_NOTIFY, out, out_len);
